{"_meta":{"openai/outputTemplate":"ui://portos/endpoint/build-918728eb79cd1f32c53f1c6c80389ab81765c99fedec688981ff4db923b6387a.html","openai/widgetAccessible":true,"ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://portos/endpoint/build-918728eb79cd1f32c53f1c6c80389ab81765c99fedec688981ff4db923b6387a.html","visibility":["model","app"]}},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Show Devices and Services"},"description":"Open the Port OS device UI when requested; never draw a second card/map/controls. Answer with the relevant value in words. This tool shares endpoint_query selection, expand and pagination. One matching endpoint opens controls; multiple matches open a selection list. It sends no control and starts no live video.\n\nprimary selects a returned cardId (for example battery, fan, closure, camera, location or house-map) and refreshes its readings; unsupported IDs return available choices. Other cards remain in details. Results include cached readings for listed cards, so avoid a second read. FRESH is current; STALE is last known with its age. Ordinary commands require no automatic UI follow-up.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"enablement":{"default":"ENABLED","description":"Filter by ENABLED (default), DISABLED, or * for both. This filter is preserved by pagination.","enum":["ENABLED","DISABLED","*"],"type":"string"},"endpointId":{"description":"Return one endpoint by its full Port OS identifier. Cannot be combined with other filters or pagination. Results advertise its declared command and outbound message IDs.","type":"string"},"expand":{"description":"Select observations to add to each device result, for example [\"power\", \"connectivity\"] or [\"battery\"]. Use capability names or full namespaces declared by the device. This reads attributes; it does not send commands or broaden the device search. Short names use port1/systems/zero/capability-interfaces. endpoint_show already includes cached readings for the cards it lists; expand replaces that selection.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"forceDeviceAttributeQuery":{"description":"Read selected attributes from devices instead of cache. Requires nonempty expand. Failed reads remain unavailable.","type":"boolean"},"maxResults":{"description":"Maximum number of results (default 10, maximum 100).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"nextToken":{"description":"Opaque cursor returned by a previous endpoint_query call.","type":"string"},"primary":{"description":"The card to lead with, one of the device's card ids (shown as cardIds in the result), for example battery, fan, closure, thermostat, camera or remote; house-map for a vacuum's map or room picking (never draw your own map). Needs endpointId. Every other card stays behind the details toggle.","type":"string"},"query":{"description":"Optional field-first filter. Omit it to load full context; filter only when the account is large. Each key is a field or a combinator, and all keys of one object must match: {\"name\": {\"like\": \"living\"}, \"type\": {\"in\": [\"LIGHT\", \"SWITCH\"]}}. Combinators: {\"and\": [query, ...]}, {\"or\": [query, ...]}, {\"not\": query}. Text operators: eq (exact), in (any of a list), like (case-insensitive substring), lt and gt (lexical order). List operators: has (contains the exact value), like (some value contains the substring, case-insensitive). Fields: id (text) returned endpoint ID; name (text) endpoint name; type (text) effective endpoint type, including customer overrides, such as LIGHT, SWITCH, PLUG or ROBOT_VACUUM; manufacturer (text) manufacturer name; model (text) model name; ownerId (text, eq only at the top level) principal whose endpoints to list; defaults to the caller; interfaces (list) full capability interface namespaces; messages (list) returned message IDs the endpoint accepts.","properties":{},"type":"object"}},"required":[],"type":"object"},"name":"endpoint_show","outputSchema":{"$defs":{"E